    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d598">

                <pb facs="0750" n="658" xml:id="pg658"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 894.85/60</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-12T16:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 12, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>[From War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 91. American requirements for steel so large that any negotiations for
                    further contracts as suggested in our No. 11, April 27 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >29</hi>],<anchor n="1" xml:id="d598-f1"/> and your No. 27, May 16,<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d598-f2"/> are now not advisable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
